#subtitle: Addressing labor unrest and strikes.

= 劳工事务

工业化的鲁尔区因劳工骚动而沸腾。雇主们已发动一场大规模的停工,以迫使工人接受更多的工资与福利削减。劳工部有必要在雇主与工人的冲突中居中仲裁。

- @support_labor: 支持工人的诉求。
- @support_employers: 支持雇主的诉求。
- @balance: 设法在双方之间达成妥协。
- @easy_discard

@support_labor
choose-if: not capital_spd or capital_spd < 10
unavailable-subtitle: <span style="color:rgb(170,150,60);font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.5px;">得了吧,伙计。你我都清楚,他们的要求完全不合理!</span>
subtitle: 这将在工人中广受欢迎,却会疏远资产阶级。
on-arrival: strike_term_seen = 1; bourgeois_power -= 0.01; labor_strength += 5; labor_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 5; workers_spd += 6*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1; dvp_relation -= 4; capital_strike_progress += 1 if dvp_relation <= 30; capital_strike_progress += 1 if unemployed > 15; capital_strike_progress += 1 if unemployed > 24; labor_goal_completed += 1; inflation += 0.1; pro_labor += 1; strike_term_seen += 1; economic_growth -= 0.1; socialism -= 1

支持劳工在社民党中总是受欢迎的,尽管我们的许多执政盟友代表雇主,对此并不怎么热情。

@support_employers
subtitle: 这将在资产阶级中受欢迎,在工人中则远非如此。
on-arrival: strike_term_seen = 1; bourgeois_power += 0.02; labor_dissent += 8; workers_spd -= 3; coalition_dissent -= 1  if coalition_dissent > 0; dvp_relation += 5; z_relation += 5; workers_kpd += 2; workers_kpd += 1 if sapd_consolidated != 1; workers_sapd += 1 if sapd_consolidated == 1; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; kpd_relation -= 8; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress > 1; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress > 8; pro_labor -= 1; strike_term_seen += 1; socialism -= 2

较为激进的工人憎恶我们镇压他们的罢工,想起了弗里德里希·艾伯特的日子。

@balance
subtitle: 在当前这场危机中,双方都得分担痛苦。
on-arrival: strike_term_seen = 1; bourgeois_power += 0.01; labor_dissent += 4; workers_spd -= 2; kpd_coalition_dissent += 1; kpd_relation -= 5; strike_term_seen += 1; socialism -= 2

许多工人对我们的妥协不满,但他们会学着接受:我们都身处一场对抗经济力量的共同斗争之中。



# options: support the workers in their demands, pushing back against the employers.
# this is the approach favored by the unions. While they do not get everything they desire, an agreement favorable to the workers is reached. The employer associations and their bourgeois allies accuse us of overstepping our bounds.
# try to make some compromise between the sides. Both sides need to share the pain in the current crisis.
# whatever it takes, end the strikes and unrest as soon as possible.
# this is not our business to intervene.
# We are the party of labor, and it is not our business to intervene? There is incredulity in the ranks. The workers are less likely to trust us in the future.
